@901 = ~Hello, adventurers. M'aiq knows many things. What would you like M'aiq to tell you about?~
@902 = ~What else would you like M'aiq to tell you about?~
@903 = ~I don't have time to talk. Farewell.~
@904 = ~Let's talk about something else.~
@905 = ~He must be from the future.~
@906 = ~M'aiq's father was also named M'aiq. Just like M'aiq's father's father. At least, that's what his father said.~
@907 = ~Dwarven mage.~
@908 = ~A dwarven mage? Impossible. Maybe later.~
@909 = ~Where can I find powerful equipment?~
@9010 = ~In the pocket of Absolute Evil.~
@9011 = ~Absolute Evil.~
@9012 = ~Many claim to deserve that title. Do your job and exterminate them.~
@9013 = ~The Twisted Rune.~
@9014 = ~Secrets, secrets, secrets... But M'aiq knows one: they like shiny rocks.~
@9015 = ~A diamond?~
@9016 = ~The little stone that helps clever beginners.~
@9017 = ~Kangaxx.~
@9018 = ~A skeleton made entirely of gold. Can you imagine that?~
@9019 = ~Demilich.~
@9021 = ~It's the story of the guy who asks people to reassemble his body even though he doesn't need it: his head is independent.~
@9022 = ~The most powerful spell.~
@90221 = ~About the most powerful spell.~
@9023 = ~Wish is the most powerful spell of the first circle: it can do anything.~
@9024 = ~Wish.~
@9025 = ~Ah, that's a spell for those who really want to do everything at 100%.~
@9026 = ~First circle.~
@9027 = ~All spells taught in the academies of magic.~
@9028 = ~Primordial enchantments?~ // if intelligence or wisdom 16+
@9029 = ~Primordial enchantments are the cantrips of the second circle.~
@9030 = ~Second circle.~
@9031 = ~Not on Toril. Mystra forbids it.~
@9032 = ~Dragons.~
@9033 = ~The dragons are here, M'aiq has seen them. They come in every color, like a rainbow. The prettiest one M'aiq saw was pink, all clean and shiny.~
@9034 = ~Liches~
@9035 = ~They should each have a phylactery... Then you could farm them.~
@9036 = ~Becoming a lich.~
@9037 = ~M'aiq does not recommend it: having your entire life stored in a box must be a truly traumatic experience.~
@9038 = ~Beholders~
@9039 = ~Do they think they are gods now?~
@9040 = ~Illithids~
@9041 = ~They hide and infiltrate everywhere, like rats.~
@9042 = ~Drow~
@9043 = ~Worse than the Dunmer. M'aiq is clever, he keeps his hood on.~
@9044 = ~Ao~
@9045 = ~M'aiq is impressed. The fact that it is possible to "become" a god in this universe is already impressive, but that it does not mean being at the top of the ladder is even more impressive!~
@9046 = ~Irenicus~
@9047 = ~He is an Imperial Guard from Morrowind, isn't he?~
@9048 = ~Bhaal~
@9049 = ~Smarter than the others.~
@9050 = ~Monsters~
@9051 = ~They are necessary, otherwise what would be the point of equipment?~
@9052 = ~Someone in particular.~
@9053 = ~Ask. M'aiq may know.~
@9054 = ~He must be from the future.~
@9055 = ~Firkraag.~
@9056 = ~Red suits him so well.~
@9057 = ~M'aiq~
@9058 = ~Good idea.~
@9059 = ~Agenor Parcilofann~

@9060 = ~Volo~

@9062 = ~Elminster~

@9064 = ~Drizzt~

@9066 = ~Bugbears~

@9068 = ~Trolls~
@9069 = ~Their skin can make fine cloaks.~

@90610 = ~Little secret~
@90611 = ~Ah, for that, ask the Secret Teller.~

@90612 = ~Little advice~
@90613 = ~Always sell to the same merchant. That way, if you later realize you sold an item you need, you will know where to find it again.~

@90614 = ~Latest rumors~
@90615 = ~They say the Black Sun fears you.~

@90616 = ~Secret Teller~
@90617 = ~You called me here. Make her come.~